  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "477209eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Model Comparison\n",
    "\n",
    "Using the same function from the untuned models, I then recalled this to evaluate the now tuned models. Interestingly enough, the Random Forest and XGBoost models performed the same. \n",
    "\n",
    "The model performs very well with Precision and Accuracy, but struggles with Recall. So, what does this mean in the context of my project?\n",
    "\n",
    "A high precision score but low recall score indicates that this model is more conservative or picky with its choices. The high precision indicates that the model has high credibility that when it labels it as pass, it passes. On the other hand, it has low recall, meaning it misses many films that do pass the test. When the model claims it passes, it's right about 73% of the time. However, of all the movies that do pass, it only found about 49%. \n",
    "\n",
    "Using this, we can say that it is much easier to determine whether a movie is going to fail, than it is going to pass. It's quite accurate when labeling it as passing, but struggles to catch all movies. "
   ]
  },
