   "source": [
    "# Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "Overall, this Sample Analysis aimed to create a model that would predict whether a movie would pass or fail what is known as the Bechdel Test. Through the steps of data cleaning, preprocessing, model tuning and evaluation, and finally model selection, these steps were carefully chosen to demonstrate the best uses of Machine Learning. \n",
    "\n",
    "The three models: Decision Tree, Random Forest, and XGBoost were all fit and compared using its Accuracy, F1-Macro, and Precision and Recall Score. The Random Forest and XGBoost models performed nearly the same after being tuned, and for simplicity sake, I chose the Random Forest Model to produce the Confusion Matrix. The Random Forest model was able to correctly identify 73% of passing movies.\n",
    "\n",
    "Using the feature importance chart, we can see that the most important features in predicting a movie's pass or fail are its number of IMDB votes, normalized 2013 budget, and release year. "
   ]
